---
import { css } from "../../styled-system/css";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import ProjectCard from "../components/ProjectCard.astro";
import { projects } from "../data/projects";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Header eyebrow="Development studio" />

  <main
    class={css({
      position: "relative",
      zIndex: 1,
      maxW: "1100px",
      mx: "auto",
      px: "5",
      pb: "16",
      display: "grid",
      gap: "6"
    })}
  >
    <section
      class={css({
        bg: "panel",
        borderWidth: "1px",
        borderStyle: "solid",
        borderColor: "line",
        borderRadius: "panel",
        p: { base: "6", md: "8" },
        boxShadow: "soft",
        backdropFilter: "blur(12px)"
      })}
    >
      <p
        class={css({
          m: 0,
          mb: "3",
          textTransform: "uppercase",
          letterSpacing: "0.12em",
          fontSize: "xs",
          fontWeight: "700",
          color: "secondary"
        })}
      >
        Software for Hive, and bridges beyond it.
      </p>
      <h2
        class={css({
          m: 0,
          mb: "4",
          fontSize: { base: "4xl", md: "6xl" },
          lineHeight: "1.05",
          maxW: "15ch"
        })}
      >
        Hivepen builds practical digital products, integrations, and tools that help people use blockchain without fear.
      </h2>
      <p class={css({ m: 0, maxW: "68ch", color: "muted", mb: "3" })}>
        Hivepen started as a software idea, but it grew into a broader development studio for helping communities,
        projects, initiatives, and individuals who want useful software connected to the Hive ecosystem and the wider
        web.
      </p>
      <p class={css({ m: 0, maxW: "68ch", color: "muted" })}>
        We believe a Hive account can be one of the easiest ways to enter crypto. Our work is focused on making that
        first step feel simpler, safer, and genuinely valuable for everyday people.
      </p>
      <div
        class={css({
          display: "flex",
          flexWrap: "wrap",
          flexDir: { base: "column", sm: "row" },
          gap: "3.5",
          mt: "6"
        })}
      >
        <a
          href="https://hive.io/es/join"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          class={css({
            display: "inline-flex",
            alignItems: "center",
            justifyContent: "center",
            minH: "3rem",
            px: "5",
            py: "3.5",
            borderRadius: "full",
            fontWeight: "700",
            bg: "linear-gradient(135deg, var(--colors-primary), #ffba52)",
            color: "#241000"
          })}
        >
          Create a Hive account
        </a>
        <a
          href="/p/"
          class={css({
            display: "inline-flex",
            alignItems: "center",
            justifyContent: "center",
            minH: "3rem",
            px: "5",
            py: "3.5",
            borderRadius: "full",
            fontWeight: "700",
            borderWidth: "1px",
            borderStyle: "solid",
            borderColor: "line",
            bg: "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7)",
            color: "ink"
          })}
        >
          Open the profile hub
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class={css({
        display: "grid",
        gap: "6",
        gridTemplateColumns: { base: "1fr", md: "repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr))" }
      })}
    >
      <article
        class={css({
          bg: "panel",
          borderWidth: "1px",
          borderStyle: "solid",
          borderColor: "line",
          borderRadius: "panel",
          p: "6",
          boxShadow: "soft",
          backdropFilter: "blur(12px)"
        })}
      >
        <p class={css({ m: 0, mb: "1.5", textTransform: "uppercase", letterSpacing: "0.12em", fontSize: "xs", fontWeight: "700", color: "secondary" })}>
          What Hivepen does
        </p>
        <h3 class={css({ m: 0, mb: "4", fontSize: { base: "2xl", md: "3xl" }, lineHeight: "1.2" })}>
          Development, product thinking, onboarding, and ecosystem support.
        </h3>
        <ul class={css({ m: 0, pl: "5", color: "muted", display: "grid", gap: "2.5" })}>
          <li>Builds software integrated with Hive and ready for future cross-platform expansion.</li>
          <li>Supports communities, founders, creators, and independent initiatives with tailored tools.</li>
          <li>Designs smoother experiences around wallets, identity, publishing, and participation.</li>
          <li>Explores ways to connect blockchain products with real-world use cases and familiar web flows.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article
        class={css({
          bg: "panel",
          borderWidth: "1px",
          borderStyle: "solid",
          borderColor: "line",
          borderRadius: "panel",
          p: "6",
          boxShadow: "soft",
          backdropFilter: "blur(12px)"
        })}
      >
        <p class={css({ m: 0, mb: "1.5", textTransform: "uppercase", letterSpacing: "0.12em", fontSize: "xs", fontWeight: "700", color: "secondary" })}>
          Why this matters
        </p>
        <h3 class={css({ m: 0, mb: "4", fontSize: { base: "2xl", md: "3xl" }, lineHeight: "1.2" })}>
          Crypto adoption improves when the experience feels human.
        </h3>
        <p class={css({ m: 0, mb: "3", color: "muted" })}>
          Hivepen is not here to talk only to developers or only to Hive users. The mission is to make blockchain tools
          easier to understand, easier to try, and easier to connect with people, platforms, and opportunities outside
          of crypto-native spaces.
        </p>
        <p class={css({ m: 0, color: "muted" })}>
          That includes helping more people discover that a wallet and blockchain account can feel accessible, useful,
          and far less intimidating than expected.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section
      class={css({
        bg: "panel",
        borderWidth: "1px",
        borderStyle: "solid",
        borderColor: "line",
        borderRadius: "panel",
        p: "6",
        boxShadow: "soft",
        backdropFilter: "blur(12px)"
      })}
    >
      <p class={css({ m: 0, mb: "1.5", textTransform: "uppercase", letterSpacing: "0.12em", fontSize: "xs", fontWeight: "700", color: "secondary" })}>
        Right now
      </p>
      <h3 class={css({ m: 0, mb: "5", fontSize: { base: "2xl", md: "3xl" }, lineHeight: "1.2" })}>
        Current areas in active exploration and development.
      </h3>
      <div
        class={css({
          display: "grid",
          gap: "4",
          gridTemplateColumns: { base: "1fr", md: "repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr))" }
        })}
      >
        {projects.map((project) => <ProjectCard {...project} />)}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
